{"id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.md","line":99,"body":"","kind":"lemma","status":"not_started","tex":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","uses":["[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz]]","[[references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy]]"],"inspired_by":[],"bindings":[],"is_index":false,"body_html":"","formal":[],"tex_content":{"path":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","line":204,"source":"\\begin{lemma}[a minimizing geodesic minimizes energy: the inequality]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality, lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz, def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy}\n\n  \\dcref{ch9:2.3}\n  Let $\\gamma:[a,b]\\to M$ be a geodesic and $c:[a,b]\\to M$ a curve with $L(\\gamma)\\le L(c)$\n  (both with integrable speed and squared speed). Then $E(\\gamma)\\le E(c)$.\n\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality, lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz}\n  \\sketch\n  $(b-a)E(\\gamma)=L(\\gamma)^2\\le L(c)^2\\le (b-a)E(c)$, the first equality by\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality}, the middle step by hypothesis (both lengths being\n  non-negative), and the last by \\cref{lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz}. Divide by $b-a>0$.\n\n\\end{proof}","html":" <p></p><section class=\"theorem\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Lemma</div></section>[a minimizing geodesic minimizes energy: the inequality] <span class=\"tex-label\" id=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368392d322d332d696e657175616c697479\"></span> <p></p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-2-schwarz\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23def%3Adc-ch9-2-2-energy\">↗ def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy</a> <p></p><span class=\"tex-source-references\" role=\"list\" style=\"display:block\"><span class=\"tex-dcref\" role=\"listitem\" style=\"display:block\">1. ch9:2.3</span></span>Let <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$\\gamma :[a,b]\\to M$\">$\\gamma :[a,b]\\to M$</span> be a geodesic and <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$c:[a,b]\\to M$\">$c:[a,b]\\to M$</span> a curve with <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$L(\\gamma )\\le L(c)$\">$L(\\gamma )\\le L(c)$</span> (both with integrable speed and squared speed). Then <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$E(\\gamma )\\le E(c)$\">$E(\\gamma )\\le E(c)$</span>. <p></p> <section class=\"theorem proof\"><div class=\"theorem-label\">Proof</div><p><a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality</a> <a class=\"wikilink tex-use\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-2-schwarz\">↗ lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz</a> \\sketch <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$(b-a)E(\\gamma )=L(\\gamma )^2\\le L(c)^2\\le (b-a)E(c)$\">$(b-a)E(\\gamma )=L(\\gamma )^2\\le L(c)^2\\le (b-a)E(c)$</span>, the first equality by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368392d322d332d67656f64657369632d657175616c697479\">section 1</a>, the middle step by hypothesis (both lengths being non-negative), and the last by <a class=\"reference tex-ref\" href=\"#node=references%2FDoCarmo%2Fblueprint%2Fsrc%2Fchapters%2FCh09_VariationsOfEnergy%23lem%3Adc-ch9-2-2-schwarz\" data-tex-node=\"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz\" data-tex-anchor=\"tex-label-6c656d3a64632d6368392d322d322d7363687761727a\">section 1</a>. Divide by <span class=\"math\" data-display=\"false\" data-tex=\"$b-a&gt;0$\">$b-a&gt;0$</span>. </p><span class=\"qed\" aria-label=\"证毕\" style=\"display:block;text-align:right\">□</span></section>","warnings":["部分 TeX 排版细节未完整还原（已保留可读内容）: sketch"]},"previous":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","next":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-smooth-variation-energy-min","relations":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy","title":"def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy","label":"def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy"}],"backlinks":[{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3"},{"kind":"uses","id":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-smooth-variation-energy-min","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-smooth-variation-energy-min","label":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-smooth-variation-energy-min"}],"copy_context":{"version":1,"level":0,"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality","tex":"\\begin{lemma}[a minimizing geodesic minimizes energy: the inequality]\n  \\label{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-inequality}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality, lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz, def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy}\n\n  \\dcref{ch9:2.3}\n  Let $\\gamma:[a,b]\\to M$ be a geodesic and $c:[a,b]\\to M$ a curve with $L(\\gamma)\\le L(c)$\n  (both with integrable speed and squared speed). Then $E(\\gamma)\\le E(c)$.\n\n\\end{lemma}\n\\begin{proof}\n\n  \\uses{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality, lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz}\n  \\sketch\n  $(b-a)E(\\gamma)=L(\\gamma)^2\\le L(c)^2\\le (b-a)E(c)$, the first equality by\n  \\cref{lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality}, the middle step by hypothesis (both lengths being\n  non-negative), and the last by \\cref{lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz}. Divide by $b-a>0$.\n\n\\end{proof}","source":"tex/references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy.tex","description":"","dependencies":[{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-3-geodesic-equality","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","title":"lem:dc-ch9-2-2-schwarz","description":""},{"node":"references/DoCarmo/blueprint/src/chapters/Ch09_VariationsOfEnergy#def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy","title":"def:dc-ch9-2-2-energy","description":""}],"dependencies_omitted":0,"unresolved_dependencies":[],"unresolved_omitted":0}}